WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:04.550
Ranging from funny to festive, these holiday
favorites are just waiting for you to binge

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:08.640
at your leisure and whenever you get started,
it'll be the most wonderful time of the year.

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.660
Here's a look at the best Christmas movie
son Netflix.

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:15.900
If you're a bit of Christmas cynic, you could
always spike your eggnog and sit down with

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:20.660
Bad Santa, a comedy about a man who uses one
of the season's most enduring symbols to gain

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:24.960
the trust of everyone around him, and then
rob them blind while also getting blackout

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:30.010
drunk. Sure, it might seem a little mean-spirited,
but Bad Santa is actually part of a grand

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:33.760
tradition of Christmas films including the
beloved classic It’s a Wonderful Life that

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:38.480
use misfortune and misery as entry points
into discovering the true meaning of the season.

00:00:38.809 --> 00:00:43.520
In this case, the person who needs to discover
it is Willie Soke, played by Billy Bob Thornton,

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:48.160
a safecracker who's sick of his life masquerading
as a mall Santa. When he meets a naive but

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:52.720
good-natured boy named Thurman, Willie finds
his life slowly beginning to take on meaning

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:57.860
again, whether he really wants it to or not.
It’s unapologetically foulmouthed and surprisingly

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:02.140
joyous by the end, and features a terrific
supporting cast that includes the late John

00:01:02.140 --> 00:01:06.540
Ritter and Bernie Mac. Plus, if you're having
fun with Bad Santa, Netflix can also carry

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:08.900
you right over to the sequel, Bad Santa 2.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:13.960
In the years since Love Actually was released,
it has divided viewers with the hottest Christmas

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:14.960
medai debate since “Baby, It’s Cold Outside.”
In the years since Love Actually was released,

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:16.160
it has divided viewers with the hottest Christmas
medai debate since “Baby, It’s Cold Outside.”

00:01:16.330 --> 00:01:21.000
Set in the month leading up to Christmas it
has a cast of… well, basically every British

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:25.680
actor you’ve ever heard of, including Alan
Rickman, Hugh Grant, Keira Knightley, Liam

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:30.540
Neeson, Mr. Bean, Bilbo Baggins and Rick from
the Walking Dead. Thanks to its interweaving

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:34.840
stories of love, it’s been called "the ultimate
romantic comedy,” and embraced as a a holiday

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:39.630
essential by many, while dismissed as an overwrought
mess by others who think it has some pretty

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:44.630
dubious ideas about romance. It's a debate
we still have every Christmas, but after all

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:47.400
that dust settles, we still want to watch
it every single year.

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:53.020
Some viewers may dismiss A Christmas Prince
as another generic royal romantic comedy that

00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:57.110
the filmmakers just slapped some Christmas
decorations on. If you actually sit down and

00:01:57.110 --> 00:02:01.240
watch it, though, you'll find charm, heart,
and a story that wrings every little bit of

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:02.860
joy out of what it's given to work with.

00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:07.520
Rose McIver stars as a young reporter eager
to catch the eye of her boss by infiltrating

00:02:07.530 --> 00:02:11.390
the Aldovian monarchy and learning what's
keeping the mysterious Prince Richard from

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:15.749
claiming his rightful place on the throne.
After going undercover as a tutor to the Prince's

00:02:15.749 --> 00:02:20.189
young sister surprise! she quickly falls in
love with Richard, only to find that there

00:02:20.189 --> 00:02:24.579
are enemies out to stop his coronation on
Christmas Eve. It's not the most lavish production

00:02:24.579 --> 00:02:28.560
you'll ever see, but there's a reason Netlfix
dropped a sequel this year. Here’s hoping

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:32.240
it becomes an annual tradition with increasingly
ridiculous plots!

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:37.579
Santa Buddies is a warm little movie perfect
for kids who love cute dogs and holiday cheer.

00:02:37.579 --> 00:02:42.450
The story revolves around Puppy Paws, the
son of Santa's dog Santa Paws (because of

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:46.620
course that's his name), who's a bit worn
out by Christmas and just wants to be a normal

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:47.120
puppy.

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:51.580
“Maybe you should be thinking about how
important Christmas is to children and puppies

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:52.840
all around the world.”

00:02:52.989 --> 00:02:56.940
Puppy Paws leaves the North Pole and tries
to learn how to be a regular puppy from a

00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:01.260
few who happen to be on Santa's naughty list.
What Puppy Paws doesn't know, though, is that

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:05.680
the very fate of Christmas hinges on him learning
a lesson about the true spirit of the holiday,

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:10.420
and he'd better learn it fast before the cold-hearted
dog catcher played by Christopher Lloyd can

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:11.280
ruin everything

00:03:11.529 --> 00:03:16.080
In other words, it’s the exact plot of Elf,
but with an adorable puppy instead of Will

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:20.099
Ferrell. Believe it or not, though, it’s
both adorable and weird enough to be watchable.

00:03:20.099 --> 00:03:24.200
The only real problem with showing it to your
kids is that they might decide a puppy is

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:25.480
the one thing they want for Christmas.

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:31.419
Get Santa is yet another film that follows
a recognizable holiday formula. This time,

00:03:31.419 --> 00:03:35.169
it’s the tale of the young child trying
to convince a cynical adult that Santa Claus

00:03:35.169 --> 00:03:39.819
is real. The twist is that Get Santa takes
that premise and mixes it up with a kinder,

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:43.870
gentler version of a Guy Ritchie crime comedy,
and the results are as strange as they are

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:44.360
delightful.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:49.460
Rafe Spall stars as Steve, a former getaway
driver fresh out of prison and eager to reconnect

00:03:49.469 --> 00:03:54.129
with his son Tom. Tom is a bit disinterested,
but calls his father for help when he believes

00:03:54.129 --> 00:03:55.680
he's found Santa inside a shed.

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:57.960
“Hello mate, how are you, how you doing?”

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:00.520
“Santa’s in the carriage.”

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:02.120
“What?”

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:06.420
This "Santa" claims that his sleigh crashed
and his reindeer have been scattered, and

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:11.100
asks for help only to end up locked in prison
instead. With Christmas on the line, it's

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:15.480
up to Steve and Tom to find the reindeer,
enlist the help of some elves, and "get Santa."

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:19.760
That is, if Steve can ever find his way to
believing in Father Christmas again. It's

00:04:19.770 --> 00:04:24.170
a wonderfully weird little movie with a new
twist on a classic tale, plus a version of

00:04:24.170 --> 00:04:28.000
the journey to the North Pole (or "Elf City"
as it's called in the film) you've likely

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.000
never seen before.

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:33.900
If you're after an enduring holiday classic
full of musical numbers, gorgeous Technicolor

00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:38.061
imagery, and the exquisite comic timing of
Danny Kaye, then White Christmas is for you.

00:04:38.061 --> 00:04:41.199
“I want you to get married. I want you to
have nine children. And if you only spend

00:04:41.199 --> 00:04:45.670
five minutes a day with each kid, that's 45
minutes, and I'd at least have time to go

00:04:45.670 --> 00:04:46.900
out and get a massage or something!”

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:51.840
Like many holiday films of its time, it doesn't
entirely revolve around Christmas, but rather

00:04:51.849 --> 00:04:55.770
builds to it by telling the story of four
entertainers who find themselves at an inn

00:04:55.770 --> 00:05:01.000
in Vermont only to find that December hasn't
brought any snow with it yet. Like the characters,

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:05.139
the audience waits virtually the entire film
for anything wintry or Christmasy to show

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:08.620
up, but when it finally does, it proves to
be absolutely worth it.

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:12.920
In addition to Kaye's comedic mastery, the
film also features Bing Crosby in one of his

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:18.449
most famous roles, Rosemary Clooney showing
both her acting and singing chops, Vera-Ellen's

00:05:18.449 --> 00:05:23.220
incredible dancing, and some of the most memorable
musical numbers you'll ever see. Oh, and there’s

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:26.360
also a pretty good song in there that you
might’ve heard of. This film has lived on

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:30.250
in the hearts of Christmas movie fans for
more than 60 years, and a single viewing is

00:05:30.250 --> 00:05:31.940
all it takes to understand why.

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:36.639
Netflix isn't just excelling in the fairy
tale princess Christmas romcom department.

00:05:36.639 --> 00:05:41.500
They've also branched out into more humble,
even somewhat quirky, offerings aimed at everyone

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:46.289
who enjoys cozy, low-stakes Christmas fare.
Enter The Holiday Calendar, the story of a

00:05:46.289 --> 00:05:51.030
small-town photographer stuck in a rut both
personally and professionally. Her life seems

00:05:51.030 --> 00:05:54.979
to be going nowhere, until her grandfather
gives her an antique advent calendar that

00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:56.580
once belonged to her late grandmother.

00:05:57.100 --> 00:06:05.740
“those are predicting the future."
"how much wine have you had tonight?”

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:10.340
The calendar will only open its doors on its
own, magically, at midnight each night in

00:06:10.340 --> 00:06:14.280
December, revealing a unique charm item that
will prove to have some meaning in her life

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:19.159
the following day. Through the calendar's
magic, Abby thinks she finds love, then realizes

00:06:19.159 --> 00:06:23.729
there are bigger lessons to be learned from
this strange little family artifact. The Holiday

00:06:23.729 --> 00:06:27.729
Calendar is, like so many Christmas romantic
comedies, is ultimately predictable, but its

00:06:27.729 --> 00:06:30.920
charm is such that you won't really care if
you see the ending coming.

00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:35.680
Sometimes the most casually enjoyable Christmas
movies arrive when you take a tried and true

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:40.020
romantic comedy formula and just sprinkle
a little holly and mistletoe through it all.

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:43.990
That's the case with Christmas Wedding Planner.
The film follows wedding planner Kelsey as

00:06:43.990 --> 00:06:48.240
she attempts to plan and execute the perfect
holiday wedding. Her biggest problem isn't

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:52.740
the venue, or the bride, but a private investigator
who's threatening to expose the truth about

00:06:52.740 --> 00:06:55.620
the couple at the heart of the ceremony and
wreck the whole wedding.

00:06:55.620 --> 00:07:00.500
“You expect me to believe that some mysterious
person hired you to ruin this wedding. "

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:04.880
“Well, technically looking at Todd, but
ah... ruining the wedding is a potential outcome.”

00:07:05.050 --> 00:07:08.360
In an effort to keep the P.I. happy while
still delivering the dream wedding she was

00:07:08.360 --> 00:07:13.150
hired for, Kelsey agrees to join his case
and help him get to the bottom of it. Of course,

00:07:13.150 --> 00:07:17.381
if you know romantic comedies at all, you
can probably guess what happens next. After

00:07:17.381 --> 00:07:21.719
a long day of shopping, this is exactly the
kind of light, crowd-pleasing holiday fare

00:07:21.719 --> 00:07:23.440
to throw on while you’re wrapping presents.

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:28.830
Dear Santa is one of the best known and most
beloved of the 21st century's large crop of

00:07:28.830 --> 00:07:34.789
made-for-TV Christmas romances that frequently
circulate on Lifetime, Hallmark, and now Netflix.

00:07:34.789 --> 00:07:39.969
It's a growing subgenre in steady rotation
for many fans, and Dear Santa is a big reason

00:07:39.969 --> 00:07:44.500
why. Amy Acker plays Crystal, a rich girl
who's facing the threat of being cut off by

00:07:44.500 --> 00:07:48.409
her parents if she doesn't find some sense
of direction. When she stumbles upon a letter

00:07:48.409 --> 00:07:52.659
a little girl wrote to Santa asking for a
new wife for her widowed, soup kitchen-running

00:07:52.659 --> 00:07:56.840
father, Crystal takes it as a sign that she's
meant to be part of their family. Of course,

00:07:56.840 --> 00:07:58.540
not all goes according to plan.

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:02.040
“I didn’t do anything, I just happened
to be here.”

00:08:02.600 --> 00:08:07.120
Netflix's devotion to original programming
led to an even bigger holiday movie boom in

00:08:07.129 --> 00:08:11.750
2018 than we've seen in previous years, and
that may have reached its peak with The Christmas

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:15.669
Chronicles, a film that blends a little bit
of The Santa Clause, a little bit of found

00:08:15.669 --> 00:08:20.509
footage, and whole lot of Kurt Russell into
a very enjoyable package. The film follows

00:08:20.509 --> 00:08:25.009
a pair of children whose family has been devastated
by loss as they try to get along together

00:08:25.009 --> 00:08:30.020
on Christmas Eve. When young Kate believes
she spotted Santa in an old family home movie,

00:08:30.020 --> 00:08:33.700
she persuades her brother Teddy to stay up
with her for a stake out. One thing leads

00:08:33.700 --> 00:08:38.010
to another, and the siblings find themselves
face to face with the real Santa Claus, who's

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:40.740
very different than decades of marketing have
made him out to be.

00:08:40.980 --> 00:08:48.600
“No need to wake up early, there won't be
any presents. You two are on the naughty list

00:08:48.600 --> 00:08:49.280
for life.”

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:54.430
With little time and a lot of frustration,
the trio has no choice but to team up, find

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:59.370
Santa's lost belongings, and save Christmas.
It’s exactly the kind of charming romp you’d

00:08:59.370 --> 00:09:03.230
expect from the producer of the Harry Potter
movies and a director who worked on Frozen

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:05.300
and Wreck It Ralph, only weirder.

